"\t\t\t\t corretas quando uma etiqueta\n"
"\t\t\t\t <replaceable> for encontrada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Working files: several files are generated when first running the tool:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Arquivos de trabalho: vários arquivos são gerados na primeira\n"
"  execução da ferramenta:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:181
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    packages.xml            auto-generated package database\n"
"    Config.in               input file for the menu driven choices\n"
"    configuration           file generated by the menuconfig process\n"
"    dependencies/*          files recording the dependency tree\n"
"    book.xml                the linearized book\n"
"    book-html/*             the linearized book rendered in html\n"
"    scripts/*               the scriptlets\n"
msgstr ""
"    packages.xml            base de dados de pacotes gerada\n"
"\t\t\t     automaticamente\n"
"    Config.in               arquivo de entrada para as escolhas\n"
"\t\t\t     controladas por menu\n"
"    configuration           arquivo gerado pelo processo menuconfig\n"
"    dependencies/*          arquivos registrando a árvore de\n"
"\t\t\t     dependências\n"
"    book.xml                o livro linearizado\n"
"    book-html/*             o livro linearizado renderizado em HTML\n"
"    scripts/*               os fragmentos de conjuntos de comandos\n"
"\t\t\t     sequenciados\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "  3.4 INSTALLED PACKAGES TRACKING SYSTEM:\n"
msgstr "  3.4 SISTEMA DE RASTREAMENTO DE PACOTES INSTALADOS:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:189
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       This tool includes a very simple tracking system to log which "
"packages\n"
"    have been installed using the tool. It is used to skip installed "
"packages\n"
"    from target selection menu and to test if an installed package has been\n"
"    updated in the BLFS book. Do not rely on this feature as a package\n"
"    management tool.\n"
msgstr ""
"       Essa ferramenta inclui um sistema de rastreamento muito simples\n"
"    para registrar quais pacotes foram instalados usando a ferramenta.\n"
"    Ele é usado para ignorar pacotes instalados a partir do menu de\n"
"    seleção de alvo e para testar se um pacote instalado foi atualizado\n"
"    no livro BLFS. Não confie nesse recurso como uma ferramenta de\n"
"    gerenciamento de pacotes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:197
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       The tracking system itself is an XML file: instpkg.xml. It is\n"
"    initialized when <make> is first run in blfs_root. It resides in a\n"
"    directory, which is created when needed during the process of building\n"
"    custom tools or blfs dependencies, right after LFS. You can specify\n"
"    that directory location in the blfs-tools sub-menu of jhalfs. You may\n"
"    need to update permissions and/or ownership of this directory before\n"
"    using the blfs tool (see README in jhalfs).\n"
msgstr ""
"       O próprio sistema de rastreamento é um arquivo XML: instpkg.xml.\n"
"    Ele é inicializado quando <make> for executado pela primeira vez em\n"
"    blfs_root. Ele reside em um diretório, que é criado quando\n"
"    necessário durante o processo de construção de ferramentas\n"
"    personalizadas ou dependências do blfs, logo depois do LFS. Você\n"
"    consegue especificar o local desse diretório no submenu blfs-tools\n"
"    do jhalfs. Você possivelmente precise atualizar as permissões e(ou)\n"
"    a titularidade da propriedade desse diretório antes de usar a\n"
"    ferramenta blfs (veja-se LEIAME no jhalfs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:204
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       The default location of the tracking directory is "
"/var/lib/jhalfs/BLFS.\n"
"    NB : after the initial build, that directory is only used to contain\n"
"    instpkg.xml, unless custom tools have been built. In the latter case,\n"
"    it also contains empty files whose name are \"$PKG-$VERSION\" for each\n"
"    versionned package built. The information about those packages is\n"
"    included into instpkg.xml the next time the tool is run.\n"
msgstr ""
"       O local padrão do diretório de rastreamento é\n"
"    /var/lib/jhalfs/BLFS. NB: depois da construção inicial, esse\n"
"    diretório será usado somente para conter o instpkg.xml, a menos que\n"
"    ferramentas personalizadas tenham sido construídas. Nesse último\n"
"    caso, ele também conterá arquivos vazios cujo nome é\n"
"    \"$PKG-$VERSION\" para cada pacote versionado construído. As\n"
"    informações acerca desses pacotes serão incluídas no instpkg.xml na\n"
"    próxima vez que a ferramenta for executada.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: README.BLFS:206
msgid "USAGE::"
msgstr "USO::"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:209
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       From now on, all the work must be done from inside the installation\n"
"    root directory.\n"
msgstr ""
"       A partir de agora, todo o trabalho precisará ser feito dentro do\n"
"    diretório raiz da instalação.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:212
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Due to the complexity of the BLFS book, the scripts and Makefile\n"
"    generation is done in several steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"       Devido à complexidade do livro BLFS, a geração de conjuntos de\n"
"    comandos sequenciados e do Makefile é feita em diversas etapas:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "  4.1  UPDATING BOOK SOURCES::\n"
msgstr "  4.1  ATUALIZANDO OS FONTES DO LIVRO::\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:220
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       If you are using the development book version and you want to update\n"
"    installed packages to the latest version found in that book, you need "
"to\n"
"    update the XML sources and packages database. To do that, run\n"
"    \"make update\". This is not necessary if you just built LFS, and you\n"
"    can skip to step 4.2.\n"
msgstr ""
"       Se estiver usando a versão de desenvolvimento do livro e quiser\n"
"    atualizar os pacotes instalados para a versão mais recente\n"
"    encontrada nesse livro, você precisa atualizar os fontes XML e a\n"
"    base de dados de pacotes. Para fazer isso, execute \"make update\".\n"
"    Isso não é necessário se acabou de construir o LFS e você pode\n"
"    avançar para o passo 4.2.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:224
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       On the next configuration run, packages already installed but listed\n"
"    with a new version in the book will be available for target selection\n"
"    and used to solve dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""
"       Na próxima execução de configuração, os pacotes já instalados,\n"
"    mas listados com uma nova versão no livro, estarão disponíveis para\n"
"    seleção de alvo e serão usados para resolver dependências.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "  4.2  CONFIGURING AND PARSING THE BOOK::\n"
msgstr "  4.2  CONFIGURANDO E ANALISANDO O LIVRO::\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:229
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       The next step is to create a book and build scripts in dependency\n"
"    build order for one or several packages.\n"
msgstr ""
"       A próxima etapa é a de criar um livro e construir scripts na\n"
"    ordem de construção das dependências para um ou vários pacotes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:233
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Run <make> to launch the configuration interface. The main menu "
"contains\n"
"    four blocks: individual package selection, Build settings, Build "
"layout,\n"
"    and Optimization.\n"
msgstr ""
"       Execute <make> para iniciar a interface de configuração. O menu\n"
"    principal contém quatro blocos: seleção individual de pacotes,\n"
"    Configurações de construção, Esquema de construção e "
"Otimização.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:240
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       In the package selection block, menus and submenus are organized\n"
"    as the book's parts, chapters and sections. You can navigate those "
"menus\n"
"    and select as many targets as you want. But we suggest to not select\n"
"    too many at a time to be able to sort issues! Note that all the "
"packages\n"
"    under a submenu may be selected at once when \"<A>\" is selected in the\n"
"    tick box.\n"
msgstr ""
"       No bloco de seleção de pacotes, os menus e os submenus estão\n"
"    organizados como partes, capítulos e seções do livro. Você consegue\n"
"    navegar nesses menus e selecionar quantos alvos quiser. Mas nós\n"
"    sugerimos não selecionar muitos de uma vez para estar apto(a) a\n"
"    classificar problemas! Observe que todos os pacotes em um submenu\n"
"    podem ser selecionados de uma vez quando \"<A>\" estiver selecionado\n"
"    na caixa de seleção.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:248
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       In the \"Build settings\" submenu, the dependency level and default\n"
"    packages used to solve alternatives are set (currently, only for the "
"MTA).\n"
"    You can also select whether the build will be made as a normal user or "
"as\n"
"    root, whether to use \"porg style\" package management, whether to "
"remove\n"
"    \".la\" files, and whether statistics for the package are generated "
"(build\n"
"    time, memory footprint and \"DESTDIR\" install). If you use package\n"
"    management, you have to enter the path to the packInstall.sh script "
"too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:252
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       In the \"Build layout\" submenu, you can select where the source "
"tarballs\n"
"    reside and are downloaded, where the packages are built, and whether to\n"
"    keep the build tree after installation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:256
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       In the \"Optimization\" submenu, you can select the number of "
"parallel\n"
"    jobs, and set the usual CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, and LDFLAGS. the special\n"
"    keyword \"EMPTY\" can be used for those flags to ensure they are unset.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:259
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Note that there are help strings associated to those menus. Please\n"
"    read them for details!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:261
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Those settings are saved to be reused in future configuration runs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:272
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       When you are done with the menu, a few checks occur, and the "
"dependency\n"
"    chain is generated. Each dependency appears with its priority "
"(required,\n"
"    recommended, optional, or external), and it's level. There is a root "
"level\n"
"    1. The selected packages have level 2. The dependencies of selected "
"packages\n"
"    have level 3, the dependencies of the dependencies have level 4, and so "
"on.\n"
"    When circular dependencies are found, they appear with a priority of\n"
"    \"circular\". This means that two (or more) dependency chains arrive at "
"the\n"
"    same package. The algorithm chooses the chain with the highest priority "
"and\n"
"    reorders dependencies to remove the other chain(s). This is not always "
"the\n"
"    solution an user would prefer, but we have found no way to do it "
"better.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       You end up with a book.xml file which contains the linearized book,\n"
"    and a rendered HTML, in the directory book-html, which you can browse "
"with\n"
"    \"lynx book-html/index.html\" (or with any other browser).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Furthermore, there is a directory \"scripts\", which contains the "
"generated\n"
"    scriptlets.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:282
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       There is yet another directory, \"dependencies\" that contains files\n"
"    generated while resolving dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:284
#, no-wrap
msgid "  4.3  EDITING BUILD SCRIPTS::\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:288
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Now it is time to review the generated book and scripts, making any\n"
"    changes to the scripts necessary to fix generation bugs or to suit your\n"
"    needs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:293
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Scripts for additional packages (i.e., for non-BLFS packages) can be\n"
"    easily inserted. For example, if you want to install the external "
"dependency\n"
"    \"bar\" before \"foo\" package and the \"foo\" script is named "
"\"064-z-foo\", you\n"
"    just need to create a \"064-y-bar\" build script.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       Remember, the package tracking system isn't a package management "
"tool\n"
"    and knows nothing about packages not in the BLFS book.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:298
#, no-wrap
msgid "  4.4  CREATING THE MAKEFILE::\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:305
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       When the build scripts are ready to be run, the Makefile can be\n"
"    created. Create an empty subdirectory (for example \"mkdir work\") and "
"cd\n"
"    to that directory. Then run ../gen-makefile.sh. Note that the directory\n"
"    is completely emptied before generating the Makefile, so to prevent\n"
"    erasing useful data, the script ensures that the name of the current\n"
"    working directory starts with \"work\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:308
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Review the Makefile, and, if all looks sane, start the build by running\n"
"    \"make\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: README.BLFS:310
msgid "GENERATED BUILD SCRIPTS ISSUES::"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:324
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      In this section, known issues with the generated build scripts are\n"
"   discussed. They are due to build procedures and/or BLFS layout\n"
"   particularities that we can't handle. In several cases, editing the\n"
"   build scripts is mandatory.\n"
"      You may also need to insert some build scripts created by you to "
"resolve\n"
"   unhandled dependencies and/or to remove some script installing an "
"unneeded\n"
"   package (unneeded packages may be pulled in the dependency chain, if\n"
"   they occur as an \"or\" with another package).\n"
"      When there are circular dependencies not known to the book (this "
"occurs\n"
"   only for optional dependencies), you may need to move around scripts so\n"
"   that they run in the order script-A script-B script-A. This involves\n"
"   copying script-A to another name (using the xxx-a- fields). Note that "
"this\n"
"   should be done before generating the Makefile in the \"work\" directory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:326
#, no-wrap
msgid "   5.1  BLFS BOOTSCRIPTS::\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:331
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Normally, bootscript installation should work. On the other hand, "
"the\n"
"     book does not give instruction for running them, so you might have to\n"
"     manually insert \"/etc/init.d/rc.d/<initscript> start\" at some place "
"during\n"
"     the build.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "   5.2  PACKAGE CONFIGURATION::\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:341
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        For those packages that have a \"Configuration\" section, you "
"should\n"
"     edit the build script to fit the needs of your system. Presently, only\n"
"     network configuration files have to be edited (wpa_supplicant,\n"
"     dhcpcd, ...).\n"
"        Sometimes, the bash startup files are modified. The scriptlets "
"contain\n"
"     a line 'source /etc/profile', which ensures that the most recent "
"startup\n"
"     files are sourced.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:343
#, no-wrap
msgid "   5.3  XORG7\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:347
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        The book has special page layouts for the Xorg7 packages. The tool\n"
"     breaks those pages into individual pages for each packages in the "
"linear\n"
"     book. Also, the menu gives the choice to select each package "
"individually.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:350
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        To build the whole Xorg7 chapter, select xinit. The (recommended)\n"
"     dependency chain brings in the whole set of Xorg packages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:352
#, no-wrap
msgid "   5.4  PATCHES\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:356
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        Please, make sure that all scripts have the commands to "
"download/apply\n"
"     the required patches. Due to book layout issues, some patches may be\n"
"     missing (as of BLFS 8.0, all the patches seem to be downloaded).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:358
#, no-wrap
msgid "   5.5  ROOT COMMANDS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:364
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        If building as a normal user (the default setting), be sure that "
"all\n"
"     commands that require root privileges are run using sudo. Also make "
"sure\n"
"     necessary root privilege commands are visible in your PATH. The "
"scripts\n"
"     ensure that /usr/sbin is appended to the user's PATH when running\n"
"     privileged commands.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:380
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        For commands necessitating root privileges, the generated scripts "
"wrap\n"
"     them with the construct:\n"
"       sudo -E sh -e << ROOT_EOF\n"
"         <commands to be executed as root with `$', ``', and `\\' escaped>\n"
"       ROOT_EOF\n"
"     The \"-e\" switch to sh ensures the command block exits with error if "
"an\n"
"     error occurs. The \"-E\" switch to sudo ensures the whole environment "
"is\n"
"     passed to the commands to be run with root privileges. It is effective\n"
"     only if the /etc/sudoers file contains `Defaults setenv', or SETENV in\n"
"     the user attributes (this is implicit if the command the user is "
"allowed\n"
"     to run is `ALL'). If you think it is a security issue, you may forbid\n"
"     this flag in /etc/sudoers, but then, you have to un-escape `$' for\n"
"     variables coming from the environment in the instructions. Although "
"this\n"
"     construct is rather strong, it can fail in some corner cases, so\n"
"     carefully review those instructions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:382
#, no-wrap
msgid "        Due to book layout issues, some sudo commands may be missing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:384
#, no-wrap
msgid "   5.7  OTHERS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.BLFS:387
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        There may be other issues that we are not aware of. If you find\n"
"     any, please report it to <alfs-discuss@linuxfromscratch.org>.\n"
msgstr ""
